; Programmable frame rotation (manual 3.12.2.4): machine XYZ = R * local XYZ + t.
; TRANS sets the offset, AROT RPL=90 turns the workpiece system a quarter turn
; about Z (G17), so local +X runs along machine +Y. ATRANS after the rotation
; offsets in the rotated system (3.12.2.1), ROT replaces the whole frame
; (the TRANS offset included), and a bare ROT deletes it.
G1 X0 Y0 Z0 F100
TRANS X10 Y20
AROT RPL=90
G1 X1 Y0 ; local (1, 0) -> machine (10, 21)
G1 X1 Y2 ; local (1, 2) -> machine (8, 21)
ATRANS X5 ; shifts along the rotated X, which is machine +Y
G1 X0 Y0 ; machine (10, 25)
G2 X2 Y0 I1 J0 ; half circle in the rotated plane, centre offset rotated to J1
ROT Z90 ; absolute: the offset is deleted, the quarter turn kept
G1 X1 Y0 ; machine (0, 1)
ROT ; bare absolute instruction: the frame is deleted
G1 X1 Y0 ; machine (1, 0)
M30
